.TH PATINA-DOCK 1 "2026-10-19" "patina-desktop 0.1.0" "Patina Desktop"
.SH NAME
patina-dock \- dock of the Patina desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patina-dock
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B patina-dock
shows the floating dock on the left of every display: the apps kept in the dock, then the
other running apps. A dot marks a running app. Clicking an app starts it, brings its window
back, or minimises it when it has focus. Right-clicking opens a menu to open another window,
keep the app in the dock or take it out, and close all its windows.
.PP
.B patina-session
starts it, and the compositor starts it again if it stops.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/patina/dock-pins
The apps kept in the dock, one desktop file name per line. Without it the dock keeps a
terminal, a file manager and a web browser, the first of each that is installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR patina-session (1),
.BR patina-panel (1)
